    {
      "id": "T02S4QRjGqiqfqgPwyFPJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 241,
      "y": -275.25,
      "width": 1300.59912109375,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 60390374,
      "version": 377,
      "versionNonce": 852566502,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785347358946,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What are services in Angular? Why do we need them?\n\n- a thingy (class, function) that can be injected into places (like components, other services) \n- Why we need them\n    - \"maintainable\" - 'testable' \n    - a source of \"state\" (data) \n        - and that needs to be shared (often) across components, features, etc. and we can't use the input output thing everywhere.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What are services in Angular? Why do we need them?\n\n- a thingy (class, function) that can be injected into places (like components, other services) \n- Why we need them\n    - \"maintainable\" - 'testable' \n    - a source of \"state\" (data) \n        - and that needs to be shared (often) across components, features, etc. and we can't use the input output thing everywhere.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
